course: dictionary
lesson: 1287
title: Plants that eat insects
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A butterwort is a small plant that catches and eats insects. Its flat, pale green leaves are sticky, so a tiny fly that lands on them gets stuck.
explain: Most plants make their food from sunlight. Butterworts grow in bogs and on wet rocks, where the soil has very few nutrients, so they get some of what they need from the insects they catch.
explain: Look at the clues in this sentence: «Butterworts have flat, greasy-looking sticky leaves that catch tiny flies.» The word catch tells you the plant traps insects, and the sticky leaves are how it does it.
fact: A butterwort is a carnivorous plant, which means it catches and eats small animals such as insects.
fact: Its leaves feel greasy, like butter.
fact: Butterworts grow in bogs and on wet rocks, where the soil has few nutrients.
fact: «Carnivorous» means eating meat or animals. A sundew and a Venus flytrap are carnivorous plants too.
fact: An adaptation is a feature that helps a living thing survive where it lives, such as sticky leaves that trap insects.
exercise: «Butterworts have flat, greasy-looking sticky leaves that catch tiny flies.» What do the sticky leaves do? | Help it float on water | Make the flowers bright | Keep the plant warm | *Catch small insects
exercise: Why does a butterwort catch insects? | It wants to share its food with the insects | Insects keep the bog warm for it | *Its soil has few nutrients, so it gets food from the insects
exercise: Which word means eating animals? | Barely | *Carnivorous | Greasy | Sticky
test: Where do butterworts usually grow? | Dry, sandy fields | Deep under the sea | *Bogs and wet rocks | Hot deserts
test: A sundew and a Venus flytrap are compared with the butterwort. What do they have in common? | *They are carnivorous plants | They are animals that fly | They have no leaves | They can only live in deserts
exam: Which statement about the butterwort is correct? | It has dry leaves that feel like paper | It is a kind of animal | *It catches and eats small insects | It grows only on sandy beaches
